Description: monitor: fall back to inotify when the fs has no file-handle support
 The fanotify monitor backend is selected whenever fanotify_init()
 succeeds (CAP_SYS_ADMIN).  On overlayfs — e.g. the privileged Athena
 build container, or any containerized deployment — fanotify_init()
 succeeds but every name_to_handle_at() fails with EOPNOTSUPP, so the
 backend cannot add a single mark and the miner-monitor test aborts:
 .
   Bail out! Tracker-FATAL-WARNING: Could not get file handle for
   '/tmp/monitor-test-...': Operation not supported
 .
 (Before the build container ran privileged, fanotify_init() failed and
 the GLib/inotify backend was silently used, which is why the suite
 passed in July.)  Probe name_to_handle_at() on the tmp dir during
 GInitable init, before fanotify_init(): with handle_bytes = 0 a
 supported filesystem answers EOVERFLOW, an unsupported one EOPNOTSUPP.
 On failure return FALSE so tracker_monitor_new()'s existing fallback
 chain picks the GLib/inotify backend — the correct behaviour on such
 systems at runtime too, not only under the test suite.
Origin: vendor, Athena-Build
Forwarded: no (could be upstreamed; upstream has since reworked monitors)
Author: Athena-Build
Last-Update: 2026-11-08
---
--- a/src/libtracker-miner/tracker-monitor-fanotify.c
+++ b/src/libtracker-miner/tracker-monitor-fanotify.c
@@ -426,6 +426,30 @@
 
 	TRACKER_NOTE (MONITORS, g_message ("Monitor backend is Fanotify"));
 
+	{
+		/* Probe for file-handle support on the tmp dir's filesystem:
+		 * overlayfs (e.g. a containerized build or deployment) lets
+		 * fanotify_init() succeed but fails every name_to_handle_at()
+		 * with EOPNOTSUPP, leaving the backend unable to add any
+		 * mark.  Fail initialization here instead, so that
+		 * tracker_monitor_new() falls back to the GLib/inotify
+		 * backend.  handle_bytes = 0 makes a supported filesystem
+		 * answer EOVERFLOW without needing a payload buffer. */
+		struct file_handle probe = { 0, };
+		int probe_mntid;
+
+		if (name_to_handle_at (AT_FDCWD, g_get_tmp_dir (),
+		                       &probe, &probe_mntid, 0) < 0 &&
+		    errno != EOVERFLOW) {
+			g_set_error (error,
+			             G_IO_ERROR,
+			             g_io_error_from_errno (errno),
+			             "File handles unsupported on %s: %m",
+			             g_get_tmp_dir ());
+			return FALSE;
+		}
+	}
+
 	monitor->fanotify_fd = fanotify_init (FAN_CLOEXEC |
 	                                      FAN_CLASS_NOTIF |
 	                                      FAN_REPORT_DFID_NAME,
